> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based on the documentation provided, here is a structured summary and guide for using the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection.

### 🚀 Overview
This project provides a collection of **16 patches** (`block 00` + `blocks 01-15`) designed to significantly boost performance on **AMD RDNA3, RDNA3.5, and RDNA4** GPUs within `llama.cpp`. It focuses on optimizing prefill, decode, and memory usage through specialized kernels and architectural fixes.

*   **Target Fork Point:** `790cf51aa` (Re-based 2026-09-13).
*   **Application Method:** Must use `git am` (via `scripts/apply-all.sh`). **Do not** use `git apply` on the concatenated series.
*   **License:** MIT (same as llama.cpp).

---

### 🎯 Supported Architectures & Benefits
The patches are runtime-selected based on GPU architecture (`gfx1100`, `gfx1150/1151`, `gfx1200/1201`).

| Family | Arch Codes | Example GPUs | Key Benefits |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **RDNA 3** | `gfx1100` | RX 7900 XTX/XT, 7800 XT | Chunked GDN prefill, WMMA Flash-Attention (576-head limit), BF16 KV. |
| **RDNA 3.5** | `gfx1150/1151` | Strix Point/Halo APUs | WMMA Flash-Attention (320-head limit), Dedicated MMVQ tables, Fused MoE support. |
| **RDNA 4** | `gfx1200/1201` | RX 9060/9070 XT | **Highest Benefit.** WMMA Flash-Attention, Chunked GDN, Hybrid All-Reduce, k-quant VDR boosts. |

> **Note:** Most features are back-ported to RDNA3/3.5. The only RDNA4-exclusive feature is **Block 12** (Hybrid HIP All-Reduce), which falls back to RCCL on other architectures.

---

### 📦 The 16 Patches (Block Summary)

| Block | Feature | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **00** | **Structural Fixes** | FA small-batch KV-split width invariance; Vulkan masked-V/freed-cell fixes. (Base for all other blocks). |
| **01** | Adaptive MTP | Adaptive draft depth (`--draft-mtp-adaptive`). |
| **02** | Chunked GDN Prefill | Fused chunked gated-delta-net kernel (bf16/WMMA). Arch-segregated kernels for gfx11 and gfx12. |
| **03** | BF16 KV & FA | Native BF16 KV cache + Native BF16 Flash-Attention. Includes HIP masked-V fixes. |
| **04** | WMMA Flash-Attention | RDNA4 WMMA FA + Q6_K mmq prefill perf. Runs on RDNA3.0/3.5 with tuned head limits. |
| **05** | CPU Purity | CPU bit-identical decode/verify batches. |
| **06** | Host Buffer Revert | Reverts host-buffer changes for discrete GPUs (now mostly a rationale marker). |
| **07** | Meta Device Skip | Skips meta device wrapper. |
| **08** | Fused-Core Prefill | Fused-core prefill kernels + GPU bit-identical results. Requires blocks 03+04. |
| **09** | Meta Buffer Headroom | Adds compute-container headroom for meta buffers. |
| **10** | k-quant Boosts | Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 mmvq VDR boosts. Adds dedicated RDNA3.5 mmvq table. <br>⚠️ **Numerics:** Changes decode numerics (VDR reordering). Not bit-identical to stock. |
| **11** | CUDA Graphs | Skips CUDA graphs for multi-token PRE-FILL (decode keeps graph replay). |
| **12** | Hybrid All-Reduce | Custom internal HIP All-Reduce for small-tensor decode. **RDNA4-only** (gfx1200/1201). Falls back to RCCL elsewhere. |
| **13** | Fused MoE | Fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + mmvq short-K item-split. Supports RDNA4/3.5/3.0. |
| **14** | Qwen4exp Support | Qwen3.8-Flash-Next support: QSA sparse FA, fused indexer top-k, HC_MIX/HC_COMBINE ops, MTP draft-head. |
| **15** | Attention Memory | **Memory Wins:** V3 derived kq mask, V4/V5 native q8_0/bf16 K/V, W1-W4 QSA memory optimizations. Saves ~3.4 GiB/GPU on qwen4exp. |

---

### ⚠️ Critical Warnings & Caveats

1.  **Greedy Purity (Block 10 & 13):**
    *   **Block 10** changes decode numerics due to fp32 reduction reordering in VDR kernels. It is **not** bit-identical to stock builds.
    *   **Block 13** also affects numerics on specific short-K rows.
    *   *If you require 100% greedy purity across builds, exclude Block 10 (and potentially 13) from `scripts/apply-all.sh`.*
2.  **Application Method:**
    *   Use `scripts/apply-all.sh` or `git am`.
    *   **Do NOT** use `git apply` on the concatenated patch file, as it will silently drop hunks.
3.  **Upstream Drift:**
    *   Patches are static against `790cf51aa`. If upstream `llama.cpp` moves, you must regenerate patches using `scripts/make-patches.sh`.

---

### 🛠️ Installation & Usage

#### 1. Prerequisites
*   A clean checkout of `llama.cpp` at commit `790cf51aa`.
*   Git.

#### 2. Apply Patches
```bash
# Clone the patches repo or ensure patches/ directory is present
# Inside your llama.cpp directory:

# Apply all 16 blocks
./scripts/apply-all.sh

# Or apply specific blocks (e.g., skip block 10 for purity)
# Edit scripts/apply-all.sh to remove block 10 from the loop
```

#### 3. Build
Standard llama.cpp build process (ensure ROCm/HIP is configured for your GPU).
```bash
cmake -B build -DGGML_HIP=ON -DGGML_CUDA=OFF ... # Adjust flags for your setup
cmake --build build --config Release -j
```

#### 4. Environment Variables & Configs
Refer to `patches/README.md` for specific env knobs. Key variables include:
*   `GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MOE_MMQ_FUSION`: Opt-out of Block 13 MoE fusion.
*   `GGML_CUDA_FA_KV_NATIVE`: Opt-in for Block 15 native K/V (default off).
*   `GPU_TARGETS`: Set during build for multi-arch support (e.g., `gfx1100;gfx1151;gfx1201`).

